cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or reproduction codebase in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Fractional Viscoelastic Kelvin-Voigt Contact Mechanics for AFM Nanoindentation of Prostate Cancer Cells"
abstract: "Investigation of biomechanical responses of prostate cancer cells (LNCaP and PC3) to docetaxel and bicalutamide using atomic force microscopy (AFM), cytoskeletal fluorescence imaging, and a Kelvin-Voigt Fractional Derivative (KVFD) viscoelastic model."
